      "answer": "May use it; perform instructions in order, skipping impossible parts and doing the rest. Cannot skip possible mandatory instructions at will (apart from permitted choices, up-to, or selecting fewer Elements consistently). May forego the whole Power; no Energy refund, and played-card Elements remain while in play.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.16-17"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q17",
      "answer": "Choose Minor or Major, draw 4 from that deck, reshuffling its discard if needed; keep one in hand, discard the other three to its deck discard. Gaining a Major requires Forgetting any one owned card (hand, personal discard, in play, even new Major); forgotten Minor/Major goes to its deck discard, Unique under panel. Forgetting in-play immediately loses Elements and unused use; previously resolved effects persist for their normal duration.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q18",
      "answer": "Damage normally means to Invaders only, distributed as chosen in target land; can combine within turn, immediately destroying pieces at Damage >= Health. Destroying Town/City produces 1/2 Fear in addition to explicit Fear. Remove/Replace generate none automatically; Replace retains prior Damage and may cause destruction if Damage meets new Health (then destruction Fear applies). Surviving Damage clears at Time Passes. Dahan are harmed by Powers only if explicitly stated.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.15-16,18",
        "FAQ Core: .bu6oczl"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q19",
      "answer": "Range boost changes reaching the target, not Gather/Push adjacency. Gather from adjacent land(s) into target; Push from target to adjacent land(s), distributing among them freely. No ordinary Ocean/off-board Push, as Ocean is not a land (specific Spirit exceptions override). Up to may be zero.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.13,19,31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q20",
      "answer": "Terror I: no Invaders; II: no Towns/Cities; III: no Cities; earning final Fear card reveals Victory and wins without resolving it. Defeat: exhausted Blight pool as instructed (or board pool empty), any Spirit without island Presence, or need to draw Invader card from empty deck. Complete current action plus triggered actions before outcome check; single-land Ravage can yield sacrifice victory if both win/loss met. Do not continue to other land Ravages before that check.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.12",
        "FAQ Core: .7w4gcs0; .bu6oc8v; .9v5kfq7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q21",
      "answer": "Adjacency is sharing a border or corner, including across boards. Coastal means touching printed Ocean, not cliff edges; other lands are Inland. Ocean is not normally a land/in play. A land is not adjacent to itself but is Range 0 of itself and hence within Range 1.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.13,31-32",
        "FAQ Core: is-a-land-adjacent-to-or-within-range-of-itself"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q22",
      "answer": "Take its four Unique cards as starting hand, follow back-panel setup on a different starting board per Spirit, choose among equally legal options, and allow multiple instructions to place in the same land. Later Presence and Powers may use any board.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.6",
        "FAQ Setup: Spirit-with-multiple-ways-to-set-up; two-setup-instructions-placing-presence-in-the-same-land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q23",
      "answer": "No, ordinarily one Spirit needs at least two own disks. Four of that Spirit’s disks in one land still make only one site. Your land is a land containing your Presence.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.13",
        "FAQ Core: .9v5ka9f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q24",
      "answer": "May select despite an impossible non-cost instruction, doing all possible instructions in any order and skipping impossible parts. Explicit cost must be paid in full. May wait for another Spirit’s Growth result; each obeys own Growth/Energy/play order and all finish Spirit Phase before any Fast resolution.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.8",
        "FAQ Core: .3y28aul; .7w4g7z1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q25",
      "answer": "Ordinary Reclaim returns all personal-discard cards to hand, not currently played or forgotten cards. Reclaim One returns one personal-discard card at any time during Spirit Phase once per phase, including the turn it is uncovered.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.14,31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q26",
      "answer": "Track Element is usable immediately whenever revealed and continuously while uncovered. Any may be selected at any time in the turn but cannot change once chosen until next turn. Forgetting an in-play card immediately removes its Elements.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.14,16,18",
        "FAQ Core: .7w4g8rf; .7w4g8p4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q27",
      "answer": "Yes, check Elements at the later threshold. Lost Elements can prevent later thresholds. Completed effects cannot be revised retroactively; Speed/Range/targeting modifications must be checked when selecting/using those attributes, and or-branch choice precedes branch resolution.",
      "source_refs": [
        "FAQ Core: .9v5kcmx; .bu6od0c"
      ]

"}

{"chunk_id":"c2655f","wall_time_seconds":0.500889306,"exit_code":0,"original_token_count":1621,"output":"{"path": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/spirit-island/2026-11-05-batch-002957/expanded-v14/answer-key.json", "byte_sha256": "c2a6caf09d768392a63ae1e3b3c3f2d6bdcc85d65c5c4929d3b33b4337e80170", "char_length": 67171, "start": 12000, "end": 18000, "slice_sha256": "a270f70016f0a913d143853e271edea00f2e01be5cdd52b0c0603b34f488d0d3", "output_cap_tokens": 5000, "truncation_check": "complete slice printed; cap >= 4000; slice <=6000 Unicode characters"}
   },
    {
      "id": "Q28",
      "answer": "Range 0 ordinarily means a land containing your Presence. A boost only extends numeric Range; it does not waive Sacred Site/source, terrain/contents target restrictions or the requirement that a land be one of yours.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.16,32",
        "FAQ Core: .3y28aqg; .7w4g8nq"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q29",
      "answer": "May target and use a legal Power even if nothing actually changes, provided it has an instruction with potential to affect game state and attempts its text. Foregoing the text is not using/targeting it. Merely modifying its own Speed/Range does not qualify.",
      "source_refs": [
        "FAQ Core: .7w4gebo; .7w4gee1; can-an-innate-power-that-only-changes-speed-or-range-be-targeted"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q30",
      "answer": "Added Town remains as a board change. Build skip expires at Time Passes. Played cards go to personal discard, all surviving Invader/Dahan Damage clears, card Elements and temporary effects clear, reminder markers removed. Track Elements remain while uncovered.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.10,16-17"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q31",
      "answer": "Damaged pieces deal normal Damage. Defend adds to 3, reducing 4 to 1 separately to land and Dahan, so no Blight and one Dahan takes 1 Damage if present.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.9,18",
        "FAQ Core: .9v5kc4h"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q32",
      "answer": "Replacement itself causes no Fear. Retained 1 Damage meets Explorer Health 1, so it is destroyed, giving no Fear for an Explorer. More generally, a piece is destroyed immediately once existing Damage meets its reduced/new Health, even without new Damage.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.15,18",
        "FAQ Core: .bu6oczl"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q33",
      "answer": "No automatic Dahan attack except Ravage counterattack or explicit Power instruction. Unqualified Power Damage is to Invaders; Dahan require explicit harmful instructions. Dahan and Invaders are unlimited; use substitutes when pieces run out.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.15-16,18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q34",
      "answer": "No; all ordinary effects remain in one target land, except explicit instructions such as Push destinations. Slash means either/both types within a combined limit: up to three pieces total, not three of each.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.16-17,32",
        "FAQ Core: .9v5kavt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q35",
      "answer": "Must move three if possible, otherwise as many as possible (two). Unrestricted Move can choose the current land and counts as movement; Gather/Push cannot because they require an adjacent land.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.17,19",
        "FAQ Core: .7w4g8of; .9v5kfr0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q36",
      "answer": "Move measures from that disk’s present land and moves up to the arrow’s distance. Add/reposition first picks a legal destination measured from any existing Presence, then may take any own island disk, even one far from that destination. It remains adding, not a Move instruction.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.14",
        "FAQ Core: .7w4g8oq; .bu6od08"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q37",
      "answer": "A Growth-gained card enters hand and may be played in the later play/pay step. A Fast-gained card merely enters hand unless explicitly permitted to play it; even explicit play does not immediately resolve unless stated. No hand-size limit; hands can be shown.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.8,18",
        "FAQ Core: .9v5kcmw; timing-of-resolving-a-power-played-mid-turn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q38",
      "answer": "Yes, effect-granted plays are additional to the normal Spirit-phase track limit. Follow payment instructions, gain Elements immediately, and use effects in its speed phase when no other action is resolving, unless explicitly instructed otherwise.",
      "source_refs": [
        "FAQ Core: .bu6ocb5; timing-of-resolving-a-power-played-mid-turn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q39",
      "answer": "Gifting/transferring is not Gain and requires no Forget. Each Major gained needs its own separate Forget, unless explicitly exempted, so one card cannot cover both. A forgotten Unique is under panel and cannot be retrieved by ordinary Reclaim/gain.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.18",
        "FAQ Core: .7w4g8pe; .7w4gee7; .9v5kc40"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q40",
      "answer": "Choose eligible Power Card when actually repeating, not necessarily at grant time. Slow cards can be repeated in Slow; these two effects specify cards and cannot repeat Innates. Printed card Elements are not granted again; explicit Elements in the repeated text are granted again.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.19",
        "FAQ Core: timing-of-choosing-powers-for-once-this-turn-repeats; .7w4g8op; .3y28aex; .9v5ka9b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q41",
      "answer": "Range/speed modifications carry over, so Repeat retains extended Range and Fast speed. Thresholds otherwise check current Elements; losing them may mean a previously met threshold no longer applies.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.19",
        "FAQ Core: .9v5kavs; Repeating-internal-range-boosts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q42",
      "answer": "Repeat instructions on a repeated Power are ignored, so repeating Powerstorm grants no Repeat permissions; its non-Repeat Energy gain still happens. Its threshold allows up to three different Power Cards, not the same one three times.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.19",
        "FAQ Core: repeating-power-cards-that-grant-repeats; .7w4g8q9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q43",
      "answer": "Explicit Repeat location overrides original Range/target restrictions, so the adjacent land can be used despite them. Original land
"}

{"chunk_id":"34e1cc","wall_time_seconds":0.846712645,"exit_code":0,"original_token_count":1622,"output":"{"path": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/spirit-island/2026-11-05-batch-002957/expanded-v14/answer-key.json", "byte_sha256": "c2a6caf09d768392a63ae1e3b3c3f2d6bdcc85d65c5c4929d3b33b4337e80170", "char_length": 67171, "start": 18000, "end": 24000, "slice_sha256": "16a4567f51651e68327c6f3acc3a393fdb001d5dc3b567c2b4e9eb96a782a77e", "output_cap_tokens": 5000, "truncation_check": "complete slice printed; cap >= 4000; slice <=6000 Unicode characters"}
 is not adjacent to itself and cannot be selected under this instruction.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.19",
        "FAQ Core: .9v5kfgr; is-a-land-adjacent-to-or-within-range-of-itself"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q44",
      "answer": "Entering existing Blight does not destroy Presence. Each new Blight addition, including cascade revisits, destroys one Presence per Spirit present and can cascade onward again. Existing Blight quantity does not multiply the single outgoing cascade.",
      "source_refs": [
