      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.15,18",
        "FAQ Core: .7w4g8r7; one-more-blight-errata"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q46",
      "answer": "Cascade remains part of original single-land Ravage action tree, not a separate outcome-check boundary. Players choose land order and may win at the end of one complete Ravage tree before another land Ravages and could cause loss.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.9",
        "FAQ Core: .7w4geg1; .bu6oc8v; .9v5kfq7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q47",
      "answer": "Determine matching eligible lands before resolving the card: initially empty land does not gain a Ravage from this card. In a land already queued to Ravage, new Invaders participate when it resolves. Players may choose any order across both terrains.",
      "source_refs": [
        "FAQ Core: pieces-added-or-moved-by-ravages-do-not-cause-more-ravages; .9v5kaam"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q48",
      "answer": "All Coastal lands across boards; later Build/Ravage likewise in Coastal lands. Normal restrictions remain: Build/Ravage only eligible lands with Invaders, Explore requires sources (Ocean provides coast access).",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.9-10,13",
        "FAQ Core: .7w4g9as"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q49",
      "answer": "No. Skipping actions in source land does not remove its Town/City or prevent neighboring Explore checking that source; the Explore action happens in the destination land.",
      "source_refs": [
        "FAQ Core: .7w4g8p8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q50",
      "answer": "Yes: just-Explored card is now in Build for next turn, so removing that Explorer before then can prevent its Build. It did not Build during that Explore. Fear cards earned in Slow wait until next Invader Phase’s Fear step.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.9-10,12,21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q51",
      "answer": "Different choices only when the card requires them; a piece may move multiple times across successive player choices if legal. Generic Presence/site conditions accept any Spirit’s; explicitly individual own-site counts use each Spirit’s sites separately.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.9",
        "FAQ Core: fear-cards-checking-for-presence; .9v5ka9n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q52",
      "answer": "May remove both Cities; Invader includes all three types and no Explorer-first rule applies. Health allowance uses current Health modifiers but marked Damage does not reduce Health.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.15,18,30",
        "FAQ Core: .9v5kaai"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q53",
      "answer": "Yes with at least one Dahan and zero buildings. Zero versus zero is not outnumbering.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.31",
        "FAQ Core: .bu6od0k"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q54",
      "answer": "Single Spirit may target itself with Another Spirit, but cannot get bonuses conditional on actually targeting another. One human playing two Spirits fills two player roles, scales by two and does not get the single-Spirit targeting exception.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.22",
        "FAQ Setup: Can-one-person-play-more-than-one-Spirit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q55",
      "answer": "Power user chooses Power decisions. Otherwise seek consensus; if impossible, land decisions belong to Spirit starting on that board, and non-land decisions to game owner/organizer.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.8 sidebar"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q56",
      "answer": "Progression is optional teaching aid. Take next listed card into hand instead of draw-four/keep-one; gaining a Major still requires Forgetting. No-card initial pool is 5 per Spirit +1 total and emptying it loses, without flip or ongoing Blighted effect.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE pp.3,6,18",
        "FAQ Core: .9v5kavp",
        "FAQ Setup: one-more-blight-errata"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q57",
      "answer": "Yes, each player chooses a different land and may Gather up to two (including zero). Then II deals one total Damage if Dahan present; III deals total Damage equal to Dahan present, not that amount to each Invader.",
      "source_refs": [
        "FAQ Core: .7w4g8rq; .7w4g8ra"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q58",
      "answer": "The Coastal City Build is entirely skipped; no Town substitute. The Town Build proceeds normally. Trade Suffers III only downgrades in Coastal lands, including when choosing a City.",
      "source_refs": [
        "FAQ Core: .7w4g8qr; .bu6ocpc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q59",
      "answer": "Single-land Power normally fixes its Defend from contents at use. Island-wide Dahan on their Guard checks current Dahan when damage occurs. Encompassing Ward follows current Presence of target Spirit, so lands gaining/losing that Presence gain/lose its Defend.",
      "source_refs": [
        "FAQ Core: do-island-wide-effects-check-land-contents-at-resolution; .7w4ganu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q60",
      "answer": "Alw
"}

